      <h2>Questions, answered</h2>
      <div class="rd-faq rd-mt3">
        <details><summary>How strong is a bamboo frame?</summary><div class="rd-a"><p>Comparable to mild steel in tension — about 84 MPa, tested to BS ISO 22157 at Swansea — while far lighter. Every joint is reinforced with flax-and-carbon lugs, and we test frames beyond their service life.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Does it crack, or mind the rain?</summary><div class="rd-a"><p>Our tubes are heat-treated and sealed with epoxy. Dry after wet rides and store indoors — the same care you'd give any quality frame.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need experience to build one?</summary><div class="rd-a"><p>No — most builders start with none. Workshop frames finish in 2 days with expert guidance; home kits include step-by-step instructions and video.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How long will it last?</summary><div class="rd-a"><p>Many of our 2012 frames are still ridden daily, 13 years on. Keep it sealed and stored indoors and it goes the distance.</p></div></details>
